{"type": "say", "text": "Good morning, Elena. Thank you. Let me start with what I can share at this stage. I've been reviewing the subpoena closely, including its incorporated definitions, and I'm in the process of preparing a subpoena-scope memorandum that will clarify the precise parameters of what's being requested. That memorandum is still in review, so I want to be measured in my recommendations today. What I can say is that the current response packet needs significant development before we submit it next month. Specifically, we need to make decisions on three fronts: first, whether to include a voluntary disclosure and, if so, at what level of detail; second, whether to propose a repayment or remediation amount; and third, what protocol we'll establish for executive interviews. My preliminary recommendation is that we should not finalize any of those three elements until my scope memorandum is complete, because the scope of records the DOJ is requesting will directly inform how aggressive or cooperative our posture should be. I'd also note that we should be careful not to over-disclose or under-disclose in the initial response -- getting the scope right first is critical. I'll have the memorandum finalized soon, and once it's ready, I can give you a much more concrete recommendation on voluntary disclosure, repayment, and interview protocol. I'd also like to hear from finance and employment counsel, as their input may bear on the scope analysis as well."}
```

